                <pb facs="0387" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg281"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Abstract—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-05-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 10,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Rockhill has seen T’ang Shao Yi. The latter says that the customs revenue is
                    already hypothecated and will not be touched; treaties and pledges will be
                    observed; the inspector-general will be an Englishman, but China will have a
                    right to control him, he being a servant of that country.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
